  "id": "781991437",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "Fortified Port Settlement on Cape St. Athanasius",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/architecturalcomplex",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/settlement",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/port",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/fort"
  ],
  "details": "<p><a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://archaeologyinbulgaria.com/background-infonotes/fortresses-cities/st-athanasius-cape-fortress-byala-varna-district-bulgaria/\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Dikov, writing in ArchBulg ca. 2015</a>, notes <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Strab.+9.5.19&amp;fromdoc=Perseus%3Atext%3A1999.01.0197\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Strabo's mention (9.5.19) of a <em>kome</em> named Larisa</a> located between <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../216904\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Odessos (modern Varna)</a> and <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../216893\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Naulochos (modern Obzor)</a>: \"\u03ba\u03b1\u1f76 \u1f10\u03bd \u03c4\u03bf\u1fd6\u03c2 \u1f00\u03c1\u03b9\u03c3\u03c4\u03b5\u03c1\u03bf\u1fd6\u03c2 \u03b4\u1f72 \u03c4\u03bf\u1fe6 \u03a0\u03cc\u03bd\u03c4\u03bf\u03c5 \u03ba\u03ce\u03bc\u03b7 \u03c4\u03b9\u03c2 \u03ba\u03b1\u03bb\u03b5\u1fd6\u03c4\u03b1\u03b9 \u039b\u03ac\u03c1\u03b9\u03c3\u03b1 \u03bc\u03b5\u03c4\u03b1\u03be\u1f7a \u039d\u03b1\u03c5\u03bb\u03cc\u03c7\u03bf\u03c5 \u03ba\u03b1\u1f76 \u1f48\u03b4\u03b7\u03c3\u03c3\u03bf\u1fe6 \u03c0\u03bb\u03b7\u03c3\u03af\u03bf\u03bd \u03c4\u1ff6\u03bd \u1f04\u03ba\u03c1\u03c9\u03bd \u03c4\u03bf\u1fe6 \u0391\u1f35\u03bc\u03bf\u03c5.\" The <em>Barrington Atlas</em> treated this Larisa as \"unlocated\" (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/2533/items/9377UUFB\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\"><em>BAtlDir</em></a> p. 345, whence <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/222103\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\"><em>Pleiades</em> 222103: Larisa</a>), but the compilation of the <em>BAtlas</em> pre-dated significant excavation on the St. Athanasius site. Dikov points out the possibility of a connection between the archaeological site and the toponym in Strabo, but is careful to state that \"no defining evidence has been found that the fortress on the Cape of St. Athanasius is in fact the fortress [sic] Larissa [sic] described by Strabo.\"</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient settlement with fortifications and port facilities located on the modern Cape St. Athanasius near Byala in Bulgaria. ",
